# The second `init` must abort rather than overwrite. rc and the project tree
# (which must be UNCHANGED by the failed second run) are the real assertions.
# stdout is ignored only because the two binaries name themselves differently on
# a fatal error: TS prints the message bare, the self-hosted binary prefixes it
# with `yo-self: error:`. Revisit at P2, when the self-hosted binary becomes `yo`.
# stdout_keep_match (P2.5 step 15): this case previously used stdout=ignore,
# which ANY failure satisfied. The kept substring is the probe-verified
# SHARED diagnostic - both compilers must emit it, so the case asserts THE
# failure, not just A failure.
stdout_keep_match=<PROJ>/probe/build\.yo already exists\. Aborting\.
